72 770 Td (OND RANDOM SECURITY REPORT \(ACADEMIC SUMMARY\)) Tj
72 756 Td () Tj
72 742 Td () Tj
72 728 Td (Date: 2026-02-04) Tj
72 714 Td () Tj
72 700 Td (ABSTRACT) Tj
72 686 Td () Tj
72 672 Td () Tj
72 658 Td (This report provides formal, conditional security statements for OND Random. The core security claim is derived from the SHAKE256-based extractor \(ONDMaxRNG\) and is framed under explicit assumptions about the source min-entropy and the cryptographic model of SHAKE256. We include a formal threat and adversary model, summarize entropy estimation using NIST SP 800-90B, and present the strongest bounds currently justifiable without external audit.) Tj
72 644 Td () Tj
72 630 Td (SYSTEM OVERVIEW) Tj
72 616 Td () Tj
72 602 Td () Tj
72 588 Td (OND Random combines:) Tj
72 574 Td (1. A raw source RNG \(OS RNG or emulator\).) Tj
72 560 Td (2. A SHAKE256-based extractor \(ONDMaxRNG\).) Tj
72 546 Td (3. OND structure metrics \(H_rank, H_sub, H_branch\) for empirical validation.) Tj
72 532 Td () Tj
72 518 Td (THREAT MODEL) Tj
72 504 Td () Tj
72 490 Td () Tj
72 476 Td (**Assets:** unpredictability of output bits, integrity of reports, reproducibility of releases.  ) Tj
72 462 Td (**Scope:** software implementation; no hardware security guarantees.  ) Tj
72 448 Td (**Assumptions:** source has min-entropy k per input block, SHAKE256 is secure \(FIPS 202\).) Tj
72 434 Td () Tj
72 420 Td (FORMAL ADVERSARY MODEL) Tj
72 406 Td () Tj
72 392 Td () Tj
72 378 Td (Let A be a probabilistic polynomial-time adversary with:) Tj
72 364 Td (- Full knowledge of algorithms and parameters \(Kerckhoffs\).) Tj
72 350 Td (- Adaptive access to output stream.) Tj
72 336 Td (- Ability to bias the raw source within stated assumptions.) Tj
72 322 Td () Tj
72 308 Td (Goals:) Tj
72 294 Td (- Predict next output bits with non-negligible advantage.) Tj
72 280 Td (- Distinguish extracted output from uniform.) Tj
72 266 Td () Tj
72 252 Td (We exclude:) Tj
72 238 Td (- Fully compromised OS/hardware.) Tj
72 224 Td (- Side-channel attacks unless explicitly modeled.) Tj
72 210 Td () Tj
72 196 Td (FORMAL SECURITY CLAIMS \(CONDITIONAL\)) Tj
72 182 Td () Tj
72 168 Td () Tj
72 154 Td (CLAIM 1: INFORMATION-THEORETIC REFERENCE BOUND) Tj
72 140 Td () Tj
72 126 Td () Tj
72 112 Td (If the extractor were a 2-universal hash Ext, the Leftover Hash Lemma gives:) Tj
72 98 Td () Tj
72 84 Td (Delta\(Ext\(S\), U_m\) <= 1/2 * sqrt\(2^\(m - k\)\)) Tj
ET
